/* Задание 37: материалы учителя.
   ABC – 30 вариантов для устной подготовки (письмо, лексика, справка, 3 модели ответа на каждый вопрос, 3 набора вопросов другу).
   RU – 18 писем о России с фразами-опорами.  QB – стимулы и три вопроса другу. */
window.W37ABC=[{"n": 1, "name": "Sophia", "g": "her", "subject": "Victory Day", "body": "… I’m doing a project on “Holidays in Different Countries of the World.” I’ve learnt that in Russia, Victory Day is celebrated on May 9th. What event does this holiday commemorate? What official events are held on this day? What do you and your family usually do on this day? … I’ve joined a local volunteer group …", "about": "the volunteer group", "vocab": "", "bg": "Victory Day (9 May) commemorates the victory over Nazi Germany in 1945. Typical ceremonies include remembrance events, wreath-laying and parades. Family customs vary.", "qs": [{"t": "What event does this holiday commemorate?", "m": [["Victory Day commemorates the Soviet victory over Nazi Germany in the Second World War.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."], ["It honours the victory over Nazi Germany in 1945 and remembers those who died in the war.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."], ["The holiday marks the end of the Great Patriotic War and pays tribute to those who fought for victory.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."]]}, {"t": "What official events are held on this day?", "m": [["Military parades and remembrance ceremonies are held in many Russian cities.", "Names a suitable official event, rather than a private family activity."], ["People attend commemorative concerts and lay flowers at war memorials.", "Names a suitable official event, rather than a private family activity."], ["There are official ceremonies honouring veterans and those who lost their lives in the war.", "Names a suitable official event, rather than a private family activity."]]}, {"t": "What do you and your family usually do on this day?", "m": [["My family usually watches the celebrations and talks about our relatives who lived through the war.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."], ["We often visit a local memorial and lay flowers there.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."], ["We spend time with our family and remember the people who fought in the war.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."]]}], "sets": [[["What activities does the volunteer group organise?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How often does the group meet?", "Asks for timing or frequency not already given in the email."], ["Why did you decide to join it?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."]], [["How many people belong to the volunteer group?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["Who leads the group?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["Where do you usually volunteer?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."]], [["What causes does the group support?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How can new members join?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["What do you enjoy most about being a member?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 2, "name": "William", "g": "his", "subject": "Defender of the Fatherland Day", "body": "… I’m doing a project on “Holidays in Different Countries of the World.” I’ve learnt that in Russia, Defender of the Fatherland Day is celebrated on February 23rd. What official events take place on this day? What kinds of presents are usually given? How do you and your family celebrate it? … Yesterday I watched a football match at the stadium …", "about": "the stadium", "vocab": "", "bg": "Defender of the Fatherland Day is observed on 23 February. Responses about ceremonies and gifts should distinguish common customs from obligatory official activities.", "qs": [{"t": "What official events take place on this day?", "m": [["Some cities hold ceremonies, concerts and events honouring military personnel.", "Names a suitable official event, rather than a private family activity."], ["Official commemorative events take place, and some organisations honour service members.", "Names a suitable official event, rather than a private family activity."], ["Public concerts and ceremonies are held in some towns and cities.", "Names a suitable official event, rather than a private family activity."]]}, {"t": "What kinds of presents are usually given?", "m": [["People often give cards, sweets or practical presents to male relatives.", "Names a suitable type of present that addresses the prompt."], ["Some families give small gifts such as books, accessories or chocolates.", "Names a suitable type of present that addresses the prompt."], ["Common presents include cards and useful items chosen for the person.", "Names a suitable type of present that addresses the prompt."]]}, {"t": "How do you and your family celebrate it?", "m": [["We usually congratulate my father and grandfather and spend the evening together.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."], ["My family gives small presents to our male relatives and has a special dinner.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."], ["We often visit my grandparents and celebrate at home.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."]]}], "sets": [[["How large is the stadium?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["Where is the stadium located?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["How do people get there by public transport?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["How many spectators can the stadium hold?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["Does it have a roof?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What facilities are available for visitors?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["When was the stadium built?", "Asks for timing or frequency not already given in the email."], ["Which teams usually play there?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["Is the stadium easy to reach from your home?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]]]}, {"n": 3, "name": "Olivia", "g": "her", "subject": "Spring and Labour Day", "body": "… I’m doing a project on “Holidays in Different Countries of the World.” I’ve learnt that in Russia Spring and Labour Day is celebrated on May 1st. What is the history behind this holiday? What official events are held on this day? What do you and your family do on this day? … A new fitness centre was opened in our city a week ago …", "about": "the fitness centre", "vocab": "", "bg": "Spring and Labour Day is linked to the international labour movement and the eight-hour working day. Present-day events and local celebrations vary.", "qs": [{"t": "What is the history behind this holiday?", "m": [["The holiday developed from the international workers’ movement and campaigns for labour rights.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."], ["Its history is linked to workers’ demonstrations and the struggle for better working conditions.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."], ["It originated in the labour movement and became a day to recognise workers and their rights.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."]]}, {"t": "What official events are held on this day?", "m": [["Some towns organise public celebrations, concerts and community events.", "Names a suitable official event, rather than a private family activity."], ["Public events and local festivities sometimes take place on this holiday.", "Names a suitable official event, rather than a private family activity."], ["There may be concerts and organised celebrations in parks and town centres.", "Names a suitable official event, rather than a private family activity."]]}, {"t": "What do you and your family do on this day?", "m": [["My family usually enjoys a day off and goes for a walk if the weather is good.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."], ["We often spend the day outdoors and have lunch together.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."], ["We tend to visit relatives or go to the countryside for the day.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."]]}], "sets": [[["Where is the new fitness centre?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["What equipment does it have?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["What are its opening hours?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["Does the fitness centre have a swimming pool?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What classes does it offer?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How many trainers work there?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."]], [["Is the fitness centre close to your home?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["Can teenagers join its classes?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What facilities are available for beginners?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 4, "name": "John", "g": "his", "subject": "National Unity Day", "body": "… I’m doing a project on “Holidays in Different Countries of the World.” I’ve learnt that in Russia, National Unity Day is celebrated on November 4th. What event does this holiday commemorate? How is it celebrated in Russia? How do you and your family usually spend this day? … My friends and I have started a book club …", "about": "the book club", "vocab": "", "bg": "National Unity Day (4 November) commemorates the events of 1612 and the expulsion of occupying forces from Moscow. Avoid confusing it with Independence Day.", "qs": [{"t": "What event does this holiday commemorate?", "m": [["National Unity Day commemorates events in 1612, when a people’s militia helped free Moscow from Polish occupation.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."], ["The holiday remembers the liberation of Moscow in 1612 by a volunteer army.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."], ["It marks the events of 1612 and celebrates unity among the people of Russia.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."]]}, {"t": "How is it celebrated in Russia?", "m": [["Some cities hold concerts, exhibitions and public events dedicated to national unity.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["People may attend cultural festivals or learn about the history behind the holiday.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["The day is marked with public celebrations and educational events in some regions.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "How do you and your family usually spend this day?", "m": [["My family often spends the day together and goes for a walk.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."], ["We usually have a quiet day at home because it is a public holiday.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."], ["We sometimes visit a museum or go to a local event.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."]]}], "sets": [[["What kinds of books does your book club read?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How often do you meet?", "Asks for timing or frequency not already given in the email."], ["How many members are there?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."]], [["Where does the book club meet?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["Who chooses the books?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["What do you usually discuss?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["Are new members welcome in the book club?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["Do you read the same book each month?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What do you enjoy most about the club?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 5, "name": "Emma", "g": "her", "subject": "International Women’s Day", "body": "… I’m doing a project on “Holidays in Different Countries of the World.” I’ve learnt that in Russia, International Women’s Day is celebrated on March 8th. What is the history behind the holiday? What kind of gifts do people usually give on this day? How do you and your family celebrate it? … My parents have bought me a kitten …", "about": "the kitten", "vocab": "", "bg": "International Women’s Day has roots in campaigns for women’s rights and better working conditions. In Russia, 8 March is also widely observed with flowers and family celebrations.", "qs": [{"t": "What is the history behind the holiday?", "m": [["International Women’s Day grew out of campaigns for women’s rights and better working conditions.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."], ["Its origins are connected to women’s labour movements and demands for equal rights.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."], ["The day developed from international campaigns for women’s political and economic rights.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."]]}, {"t": "What kind of gifts do people usually give on this day?", "m": [["People often give flowers, chocolates and small personal gifts.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Common gifts include bouquets, sweets and thoughtful presents.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Many families choose flowers, cards or chocolates for women they want to congratulate.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "How do you and your family celebrate it?", "m": [["We usually give my mum flowers and have a family meal.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."], ["My family congratulates my mother and grandmother and spends the day together.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."], ["We often visit our grandparents and give the women in our family small presents.", "Describes a family practice rather than only a general tradition."]]}], "sets": [[["What is your kitten’s name?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How old is the kitten?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["What colour is its fur?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["Where does the kitten usually sleep?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["What food does it like?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Who looks after it when you are away?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."]], [["Is the kitten playful?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What toys does it enjoy?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Does it get along with other pets?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]]]}, {"n": 6, "name": "Emily", "g": "her", "subject": "Children", "body": "… Next weekend my aunt is coming to my place together with all her children. What did you enjoy doing as a child? What was your favourite toy when you were a child? Do you think it is better for children to live in the city or in the countryside? Last month I made some changes to the decoration of my room …", "about": "the changes she made in her room", "vocab": "", "bg": "This task invites a personal or contextual answer about children. Use concrete examples, not unsupported universal claims. Distinguish your own experience from national facts.", "qs": [{"t": "What did you enjoy doing as a child?", "m": [["I loved riding my bike and playing outside with my friends.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["As a child, I enjoyed drawing and making up stories.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I used to spend hours building things with blocks and playing board games.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What was your favourite toy when you were a child?", "m": [["My favourite toy was a teddy bear because I took it everywhere.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["I loved my toy train; I played with it almost every day.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["My favourite was a set of building blocks because I could create different things.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."]]}, {"t": "Do you think it is better for children to live in the city or in the countryside?", "m": [["I think the countryside is better for young children because they have more space to play outdoors.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I would choose the city because children can attend different clubs and activities.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Both have advantages, but I prefer the countryside for its cleaner air and quieter environment.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}], "sets": [[["What did you change in your room?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Why did you make those changes?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."], ["Did anyone help you with the decorating?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]], [["What colours did you choose for the room?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Did you buy any new furniture?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["How long did the changes take?", "Asks for duration related to the target."]], [["Which part of the room looks most different now?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["Did you move the furniture yourself?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What do you like most about the result?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 7, "name": "Kevin", "g": "his", "subject": "Reading preferences", "body": "… Last week I went to a book festival. It was fantastic! We spent two hours looking through new books and talking to authors. What is the last book you’ve read? What books do you have to read for your literature classes? How often do you spend time reading a book for pleasure? I saw an interesting film in Spanish last week …", "about": "the film", "vocab": "", "bg": "For book-related answers, name a genuine title and author if possible. A personal reading preference is not an objective fact that needs to be memorised.", "qs": [{"t": "What is the last book you’ve read?", "m": [["The last book I read was The Hobbit, and I enjoyed its adventurous plot.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I recently finished Harry Potter and the Philosopher’s Stone; it was exciting.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["My latest book was a detective story, which kept me interested until the end.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What books do you have to read for your literature classes?", "m": [["We have to read several Russian classics, including works by Pushkin and Gogol.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["For literature, we study novels, poems and plays by Russian authors.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Our reading list includes classic Russian fiction and poetry.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "How often do you spend time reading a book for pleasure?", "m": [["I usually read for pleasure a few times a week, especially in the evening.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["I try to read for about twenty minutes every day.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["I mainly read at weekends because school keeps me busy.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."]]}], "sets": [[["What is the Spanish film about?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Who plays the main character?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["Did you enjoy the ending?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]], [["What is the title of the film?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Where did you watch it?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["Would you recommend it to me?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["What genre does the film belong to?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How long is it?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["What did you like most about it?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 8, "name": "Marion", "g": "her", "subject": "Foreign languages", "body": "… They say that Russian students can choose a foreign language to study at school. Do many students choose other languages instead of English? Why do you think they do so? Why have you chosen English?... I’ve just finished reading a collection of Anton Chekhov’s short stories...", "about": "the book she has just finished reading", "vocab": "", "bg": "Questions about foreign-language study need to distinguish national tendencies from the student’s own choices. Avoid absolute statements about all Russian schools.", "qs": [{"t": "Do many students choose other languages instead of English?", "m": [["English is the main foreign language at many schools, although some students study German or French.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Most pupils I know learn English, but a smaller number choose other languages.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["English is very common, while German, French and Chinese are also studied in some schools.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "Why do you think they do so?", "m": [["Some choose another language because they are interested in its culture.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["They may need a language for future studies, work or travel.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["Sometimes their school offers a particular language, or their parents encourage them to learn it.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}, {"t": "Why have you chosen English?", "m": [["I chose English because it helps me communicate with people from other countries.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I study English because I want to travel and understand films in the original language.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I picked English because it may be useful for university and my future career.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}], "sets": [[["What is the title of the Chekhov collection?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Which story did you like best?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["What did you think of the ending of that story?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["How many stories did the collection contain?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["Why did you choose this book?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."], ["Was the language difficult to understand?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]], [["Who was your favourite character in the collection?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["How long did it take you to finish it?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["Would you recommend the collection to a friend?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]]]}, {"n": 9, "name": "Kelly", "g": "her", "subject": "Russian traditions", "body": "… They say that Russian New Year traditions are unique. How do Russians celebrate the New Year? What are some special New Year dishes? How does your family celebrate the New Year? I’ve decided to start learning Russian...", "about": "her decision to start learning Russian", "vocab": "", "bg": "New Year is a major family holiday in Russia. Examples of festive food may include Olivier salad and mandarins; individual traditions differ.", "qs": [{"t": "How do Russians celebrate the New Year?", "m": [["Many Russians celebrate New Year with a festive dinner and watch the countdown to midnight.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Families often decorate a New Year tree and exchange presents.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["People usually gather with relatives or friends and celebrate when the clock strikes twelve.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What are some special New Year dishes?", "m": [["Salads such as Olivier and herring under a fur coat are traditional New Year dishes.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Many tables include Olivier salad, mandarins and various festive dishes.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Families often prepare salads, baked meat and other special food for the celebration.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "How does your family celebrate the New Year?", "m": [["We decorate our home, cook a festive meal and exchange gifts.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["My family usually stays at home and watches the New Year celebrations together.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["We invite relatives for dinner and celebrate at midnight.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}], "sets": [[["Why did you decide to learn Russian?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."], ["How are you planning to study it?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["What would you like to learn first?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["Are you going to have a Russian teacher?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What materials will you use?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How much time will you spend studying each week?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["What interests you most about the Russian language?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Would you like to practise with a language partner?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["What do you think will be most challenging?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 10, "name": "Simon", "g": "his", "subject": "Computer games", "body": "… I know that the Russian team won The International 10 – world cyber sport championship in 2021. What computer games are most popular with Russian teenagers? How much time do you and your friends spend playing computer games? What else do you use your computer for? I spend too much time surfing the internet and I’m thinking of joining our school sports club...", "about": "his school sports club", "vocab": "", "bg": "Popularity of computer games changes over time. Present examples as illustrations rather than verified nationwide rankings.", "qs": [{"t": "What computer games are most popular with Russian teenagers?", "m": [["Games such as Minecraft and popular football simulators are widely played by teenagers.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Many young people enjoy online multiplayer and mobile games.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Among people I know, sandbox games and team-based online games are particularly popular.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "How much time do you and your friends spend playing computer games?", "m": [["My friends and I usually play for about an hour after homework.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I rarely play on school days, but I sometimes play for two hours at weekends.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["We spend a little time gaming in the evening, although schoolwork comes first.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What else do you use your computer for?", "m": [["I also use my computer to study, research topics and make presentations.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I often use it for video calls, school assignments and editing photos.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Apart from gaming, I use my computer for language learning and watching educational videos.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}], "sets": [[["What sports can students do at your school sports club?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How often does the club meet?", "Asks for timing or frequency not already given in the email."], ["Who coaches the members?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."]], [["Where does the sports club train?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["Can beginners join the club?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["How many students belong to it?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."]], [["Does the club take part in competitions?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What equipment does it provide?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["What do you like most about the club?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 11, "name": "Mark", "g": "his", "subject": "Inventions", "body": "… Last week we went to the science museum in Chicago with my classmates. We learned a lot about modern inventions. What is the most useful modern invention in your opinion? What museums do you like going to, if any? How often do you go on excursions to museums with your classmates? I spent hours working on a group project last week …", "about": "his group project", "vocab": "", "bg": "Modern invention questions ask for an opinion supported by a concrete function or benefit; there is no one officially prescribed invention.", "qs": [{"t": "What is the most useful modern invention in your opinion?", "m": [["I think the smartphone is one of the most useful inventions because it combines communication and navigation.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["In my opinion, the internet is especially useful because it gives people access to information.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I would choose GPS technology because it helps people travel safely and find places.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What museums do you like going to, if any?", "m": [["I enjoy science museums because their interactive exhibits are interesting.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I like visiting history museums as they help me understand the past.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Art museums are my favourite because I enjoy looking at paintings.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "How often do you go on excursions to museums with your classmates?", "m": [["Our class goes to museums about once or twice a year.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["We usually visit a museum once a term.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["We rarely go on class excursions, perhaps once a year.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."]]}], "sets": [[["What was your group project about?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How many students were in your group?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["What was your role in it?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["How long did you work on the project?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["What sources did you use?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Which part was the most difficult?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["Who organised the project?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["How did you divide the work?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["What did you learn from doing it?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 12, "name": "Harley", "g": "his", "subject": "Family", "body": "… For the first time in my life, I’ve participated in a school swimming competition, and my family supported me so much! What’s the best thing about your family? What do you usually talk to your parents about? Do you prefer spending your free time with family or friends and why? I’m going to a summer arts camp in August …", "about": "the summer arts camp", "vocab": "", "bg": "This task invites a personal or contextual answer about family. Use concrete examples, not unsupported universal claims. Distinguish your own experience from national facts.", "qs": [{"t": "What’s the best thing about your family?", "m": [["The best thing about my family is that we always support one another.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I love the fact that we can talk openly and have fun together.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["My favourite thing is how my family helps me when I have a problem.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What do you usually talk to your parents about?", "m": [["We usually discuss school, our plans and what happened during the day.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["I talk to my parents about my friends, homework and future studies.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["We often chat about films, family news and everyday problems.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."]]}, {"t": "Do you prefer spending your free time with family or friends and why?", "m": [["I prefer spending free time with friends because we share similar interests.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I usually choose family time because I feel relaxed and supported at home.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["It depends: I enjoy meeting friends, but I also value family evenings.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}], "sets": [[["Where will the summer arts camp take place?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["How long will you stay there?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["What art activities will you do?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["Who will teach the classes at the camp?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["Will you stay in shared rooms?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["Are you going there with friends?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]], [["What kind of art will you focus on?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How many students are expected?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["Will you display your work at the end?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]]]}, {"n": 13, "name": "Oscar", "g": "his", "subject": "Food", "body": "… My mom decided that now we have to eat only healthy food, and I totally agree with her! What do you eat for breakfast? What is your favourite food? What do you think about fast food? Yesterday I started reading a book about happiness …", "about": "the book", "vocab": "", "bg": "This task invites a personal or contextual answer about food. Use concrete examples, not unsupported universal claims. Distinguish your own experience from national facts.", "qs": [{"t": "What do you eat for breakfast?", "m": [["I usually have porridge and fruit for breakfast.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["I often eat eggs and toast before school.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["My usual breakfast is yoghurt with cereal and a cup of tea.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."]]}, {"t": "What is your favourite food?", "m": [["My favourite food is pasta because it is delicious and easy to prepare.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I love homemade dumplings, especially when my family cooks them together.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["My favourite dish is vegetable soup because it is warming and tasty.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What do you think about fast food?", "m": [["I think fast food is convenient, but people should not eat it too often.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["Fast food can be tasty, although I prefer homemade meals because they are healthier.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["I do not mind eating fast food occasionally, but a balanced diet is important.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."]]}], "sets": [[["What is the book about?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Who wrote it?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["Why did you choose it?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."]], [["What is the title of the book?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Who is your favourite character?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["Would you recommend it?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["How long is the book?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["What is its main message?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Which part do you find most interesting?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]]]}, {"n": 14, "name": "Emily", "g": "her", "subject": "Camping", "body": "… All of my friends think camping is a perfect way to spend the holidays. What is your attitude to camping? Is it popular with Russian teenagers, and why or why not? What are the best ways to spend the holidays for you and your friends? I’ve just started watching an interesting TV show …", "about": "the TV show", "vocab": "", "bg": "This task invites a personal or contextual answer about camping. Use concrete examples, not unsupported universal claims. Distinguish your own experience from national facts.", "qs": [{"t": "What is your attitude to camping?", "m": [["I enjoy camping because it lets me spend time in nature.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Camping sounds exciting, but I prefer comfortable accommodation.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I think camping is a great way to relax outdoors and learn practical skills.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "Is it popular with Russian teenagers, and why or why not?", "m": [["It is quite popular with some Russian teenagers because they enjoy hiking and being outdoors.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["Many teenagers like camping, although others prefer hotels and city breaks.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I think it is popular among outdoor enthusiasts because it is adventurous and often affordable.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}, {"t": "What are the best ways to spend the holidays for you and your friends?", "m": [["My friends and I prefer travelling to new places and exploring them on foot.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["For us, a holiday is best spent swimming, sightseeing and relaxing.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["We enjoy going to the countryside, cycling and spending time together.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}], "sets": [[["What is the TV show about?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Who is your favourite character?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["How often do new episodes appear?", "Asks for timing or frequency not already given in the email."]], [["What is the show called?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["What genre is it?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Why did you decide to watch it?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."]], [["How many episodes have you watched so far?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["Who stars in it?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["Would you recommend it to me?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]]]}, {"n": 15, "name": "Jessica", "g": "her", "subject": "Holidays", "body": "… Hurrah! Summer is finally here. Do you spend your summer holidays with your family or your friends? Where do you usually spend your holidays? Why do you think some people enjoy spending holidays where they live? My brother Tim has just passed his exams...", "about": "the exams", "vocab": "", "bg": "This task invites a personal or contextual answer about holidays. Use concrete examples, not unsupported universal claims. Distinguish your own experience from national facts.", "qs": [{"t": "Do you spend your summer holidays with your family or your friends?", "m": [["I usually spend part of my summer holidays with my family and part with friends.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I mostly travel with my parents, although I often meet friends at home.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I prefer spending summer with friends, but I also take family trips.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "Where do you usually spend your holidays?", "m": [["I usually spend my holidays in the countryside with my grandparents.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["My family often goes to the seaside for a week or two.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["I normally stay in my hometown and sometimes visit relatives.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."]]}, {"t": "Why do you think some people enjoy spending holidays where they live?", "m": [["Some people enjoy staying at home because it is inexpensive and relaxing.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["They may want to explore their local area without travelling far.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["A holiday at home can be comfortable because people can rest and spend time with family.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}], "sets": [[["Which exams did your brother take?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["Which one did he find hardest?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["How did he prepare for them?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["How many exams did he sit?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["Which subject did he feel most confident about?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["How did he celebrate afterwards?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["Did he take any optional exams?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["How long did he spend revising?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["Was he nervous before the exams?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]]]}, {"n": 16, "name": "Sam", "g": "his", "subject": "Work or study", "body": "… I really don’t know whether to enter a college or to start working after finishing school. What are your plans? Do many Russian school-leavers continue their education in universities, why? Where can a teenager work in Russia after finishing school? My elder sister is getting married next week, it will be a big wedding...", "about": "his sister’s wedding", "vocab": "", "bg": "Post-school routes vary: university, college, vocational training and work. Avoid suggesting that every teenager follows the same route.", "qs": [{"t": "What are your plans?", "m": [["I plan to go to university and study computer science after school.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["After school I hope to enter university and train as a teacher.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I would like to continue my education, although I am still choosing a course.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "Do many Russian school-leavers continue their education in universities, why?", "m": [["Yes, many school-leavers enter universities because they want qualifications for their careers.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["A considerable number do, as higher education is important for many professions.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["Many continue studying because they hope to develop specialist skills and improve their job prospects.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}, {"t": "Where can a teenager work in Russia after finishing school?", "m": [["A teenager might work in a café, shop or delivery service, depending on age and employment rules.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["Some school-leavers find entry-level jobs in retail or hospitality.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["After finishing school, teenagers may look for work as assistants in shops or cafés.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."]]}], "sets": [[["Where will your sister’s wedding take place?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["How many guests are coming?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["What are you going to wear to the wedding?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["Who is organising the wedding?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["Will there be a big reception?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What music have they chosen?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["What time will the ceremony begin?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Will the wedding be indoors or outdoors?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["Are you going to give a speech?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]]]}, {"n": 17, "name": "Harry", "g": "his", "subject": "Animal protection", "body": "… Last month our class went to the zoo to find out about the animal conservation programme. Are there any endangered animals in Russia and what are these? Do you consider helping animals important, why or why not? What can people do to help endangered species? I’ve just finished reading an interesting novel …", "about": "the novel", "vocab": "", "bg": "Examples of threatened species in Russia include the Amur leopard. Conservation measures include habitat protection and anti-poaching work.", "qs": [{"t": "Are there any endangered animals in Russia and what are these?", "m": [["Yes, Russia has endangered species such as the Amur leopard and the Siberian tiger.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Some rare animals in Russia include the Amur leopard and the snow leopard.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["The Amur tiger and several other species need protection in Russia.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "Do you consider helping animals important, why or why not?", "m": [["Yes, helping animals is important because biodiversity keeps ecosystems healthy.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I think we should protect animals because people are responsible for much habitat destruction.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["Definitely: saving species helps maintain the balance of nature.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}, {"t": "What can people do to help endangered species?", "m": [["People can protect habitats, support conservation projects and reduce pollution.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["They can donate to wildlife charities and avoid buying products made from endangered animals.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Stronger nature reserves and education can help endangered species survive.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}], "sets": [[["What is the novel about?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Who wrote it?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["Who was your favourite character?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."]], [["What is the title of the novel?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Why did you choose to read it?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."], ["What did you think of the ending?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["What genre is the novel?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How long did it take you to read it?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["Would you recommend it?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]]]}, {"n": 18, "name": "Lily", "g": "her", "subject": "Summer holidays", "body": "… School is over! Holidays are looming on the horizon, hurrah! Where do Russian teenagers spend their summer holidays? What entertainment is popular among them? How do you prefer to spend your free time? I took all my final exams last week …", "about": "her school-leaving exams", "vocab": "", "bg": "Summer holidays vary across families and regions. Give examples rather than universal claims about Russian teenagers.", "qs": [{"t": "Where do Russian teenagers spend their summer holidays?", "m": [["Many Russian teenagers spend their summer holidays at home, in the countryside or at the seaside.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["Some stay with grandparents, while others travel with their families.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["Teenagers often spend time in their hometowns or visit holiday camps.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."]]}, {"t": "What entertainment is popular among them?", "m": [["Popular activities include cycling, swimming, gaming and meeting friends.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Many enjoy outdoor sports, trips to the cinema and socialising.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Young people often go for walks, play sports or watch films together.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "How do you prefer to spend your free time?", "m": [["I prefer meeting friends, reading and going for bike rides.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["In my free time I enjoy drawing, listening to music and walking.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["I usually relax by playing sport or spending time with my friends.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."]]}], "sets": [[["Which school-leaving exams did you take?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["Which exam was the most difficult?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["How did you prepare for them?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["How many exams did you sit?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["Which subject did you enjoy revising most?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["How did you feel after your last exam?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["Did you take any optional exams?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["How long did your revision take?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["What advice would you give someone preparing for the same exams?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 19, "name": "Dave", "g": "his", "subject": "PE classes", "body": "… Our PE teacher is super! He lets us play different ball games and sports during the lessons. Do you like your PE classes, and why? What sports and games can you play at school? What after-class activities are most popular in your school? Last week my Dad organized a picnic for all our family …", "about": "the family picnic", "vocab": "", "bg": "This task invites a personal or contextual answer about pe classes. Use concrete examples, not unsupported universal claims. Distinguish your own experience from national facts.", "qs": [{"t": "Do you like your PE classes, and why?", "m": [["Yes, I like PE because it helps me stay fit and gives me a break from studying.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I enjoy PE because team games are fun, although running is not my favourite.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["PE is useful, but I prefer some activities to others because I am not very sporty.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}, {"t": "What sports and games can you play at school?", "m": [["We can play volleyball, basketball and football at school.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Our PE lessons include athletics, badminton and team games.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["At my school we do running, gymnastics and various ball games.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What after-class activities are most popular in your school?", "m": [["Football and volleyball clubs are popular among students at my school.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Many students attend art, music and sports clubs after lessons.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Our most popular activities are sports clubs and extra classes in creative subjects.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}], "sets": [[["Where did your family have the picnic?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["Who came with you?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["What food did you take?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["How long did the picnic last?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["What games did you play?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Did you enjoy the day?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]], [["Why did your father choose that place?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."], ["What was the weather like?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["What did you like most about the picnic?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 20, "name": "Mike", "g": "his", "subject": "Mobile devices", "body": "… I’ve recently been involved in a school survey on gadgets and devices. What device is your favourite, if any? What do you usually use it for? Do you consider using mobile phones essential for young people, why or why not? I’ve recently returned from a nice summer camp …", "about": "the summer camp", "vocab": "", "bg": "This task invites a personal or contextual answer about mobile devices. Use concrete examples, not unsupported universal claims. Distinguish your own experience from national facts.", "qs": [{"t": "What device is your favourite, if any?", "m": [["My favourite device is my smartphone because it is useful every day.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I like my laptop best because it helps me study and work on projects.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["My favourite is my tablet as I can read and draw on it.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What do you usually use it for?", "m": [["I use it to communicate with friends and check my homework.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["I mostly use it for studying, listening to music and watching videos.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["It helps me find information, use maps and keep in touch with family.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."]]}, {"t": "Do you consider using mobile phones essential for young people, why or why not?", "m": [["Yes, phones are useful for communication and safety, although screen time needs limits.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I think phones are important because teenagers use them for school and contacting parents.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["They are helpful but not essential every minute; people should also spend time offline.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}], "sets": [[["Where is the summer camp located?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["How long will you stay there?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["What activities does it offer?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["Are any of your friends going to the camp?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What accommodation is provided?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Who organises the camp?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."]], [["What sports can you do at the camp?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How many teenagers usually attend?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["What are you looking forward to most?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 21, "name": "Oscar", "g": "his", "subject": "Russian literature", "body": "… Yesterday at school our foreign language teacher told us a lot about Russian literature. What Russian writers are popular with Russian teenagers? Who is your favourite writer? What book of Russian literature do you think a foreigner should read first, and why? I’ve just got an unusual present …", "about": "the present", "vocab": "", "bg": "Distinguish curriculum classics, e.g. Pushkin and Gogol, from an unsupported claim about all teenagers’ personal favourites.", "qs": [{"t": "What Russian writers are popular with Russian teenagers?", "m": [["Pushkin and Gogol are studied widely, and some teenagers also enjoy modern Russian fiction.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Many pupils read writers such as Pushkin, Tolstoy and Chekhov at school.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Russian classics like Pushkin and Dostoevsky are well known, although tastes vary.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "Who is your favourite writer?", "m": [["My favourite writer is Pushkin because his stories and poems are memorable.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I especially enjoy Chekhov because his short stories explore people’s behaviour.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I like Gogol because his writing is imaginative and often humorous.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What book of Russian literature do you think a foreigner should read first, and why?", "m": [["I would recommend Pushkin’s The Captain’s Daughter because it has an engaging story and historical setting.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["A foreign reader could start with Chekhov’s short stories because they are relatively short and insightful.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I would choose Gogol’s The Overcoat because it introduces important themes in Russian literature.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}], "sets": [[["What present did you buy for your brother?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Why did you choose it?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."], ["Where did you buy it?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."]], [["What colour is the present?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Does your brother need it for a particular hobby?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["How are you going to wrap it?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["Was the present difficult to find?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What does it look like?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["When are you planning to give it to him?", "Asks for timing or frequency not already given in the email."]]]}, {"n": 22, "name": "Patrick", "g": "his", "subject": "A lesson to remember", "body": "… At school we talked about the events in the history of our country that we can be proud of. What is the event in the history of Russia that you are most proud of? What historical person do you think best represents the values of your country? Why is it important to know the history of your country? During the holidays my friends and I always help our local environment protection organizations …", "about": "the local environment protection organizations", "vocab": "", "bg": "Historical figures and important events may be matters of personal choice; the answer needs a named example and a reason.", "qs": [{"t": "What is the event in the history of Russia that you are most proud of?", "m": [["I am especially proud of the victory over Nazi Germany in 1945 because it came at a huge human cost.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."], ["I admire the first human space flight in 1961 because it was a scientific breakthrough.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."], ["I am proud of major Russian achievements in space exploration, especially Gagarin’s flight.", "Identifies the historical event or origin requested."]]}, {"t": "What historical person do you think best represents the values of your country?", "m": [["I would choose Yuri Gagarin because his courage and determination inspired many people.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["In my opinion, scientist Mikhail Lomonosov represents curiosity and commitment to education.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I think Yuri Gagarin represents courage and the desire to discover new things.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "Why is it important to know the history of your country?", "m": [["History helps us understand how the present was shaped.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["It is important because learning about past mistakes can guide future decisions.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["Knowing history helps people understand their culture and respect different perspectives.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}], "sets": [[["What do the local environmental organisations do?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How can young people join them?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["Where do they usually organise events?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."]], [["Which environmental problems do the organisations focus on?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["How often do their volunteers meet?", "Asks for timing or frequency not already given in the email."], ["Do they work with local schools?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]], [["What campaigns are they running at the moment?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Who coordinates the volunteers?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["What results have the organisations achieved recently?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 23, "name": "Sandra", "g": "her", "subject": "Food preferences", "body": "… Nowadays I always try to eat healthy food. But in the past, I used to love sweets and fast food very much. What kind of food do Russian people eat most often? How have your food preferences changed since you were a kid? Do you think your food preferences will continue to change as you get older, why or why not? My family and I still write letters to Santa at Christmas …", "about": "her letters to Santa", "vocab": "", "bg": "This task invites a personal or contextual answer about food preferences. Use concrete examples, not unsupported universal claims. Distinguish your own experience from national facts.", "qs": [{"t": "What kind of food do Russian people eat most often?", "m": [["Many people in Russia often eat soups, porridge, potatoes and home-cooked meals.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Common everyday foods include soup, cereals, vegetables and meat or fish.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Families frequently prepare dishes such as buckwheat, soup and dumplings.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "How have your food preferences changed since you were a kid?", "m": [["As a child I preferred sweets, but now I enjoy more vegetables and savoury food.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I used to dislike fish, but I have started eating it more often.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["My tastes have changed because I now prefer home-cooked food to fast food.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "Do you think your food preferences will continue to change as you get older, why or why not?", "m": [["Yes, I think my tastes will change as I try new dishes and learn more about nutrition.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["Probably, because people often discover different foods as they grow older.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I expect so: travel and new experiences may introduce me to different cuisines.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}], "sets": [[["What do you usually write in your letters to Santa?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["When do you normally write them?", "Asks for timing or frequency not already given in the email."], ["Do you decorate the letters?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]], [["What was the most unusual thing you asked Santa for?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Where do you put your letters?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["Do your family members help you write them?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]], [["How long have you had this tradition?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["What language do you write the letters in?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Which letter do you remember best?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]]]}, {"n": 24, "name": "Lily", "g": "her", "subject": "Hobbies", "body": "… Many of my friends enjoy roller-skating in their free time, and I like it too. How do you and your friends spend free time in your region? Which hobbies are popular with teens in Russia? What new hobby would you like to try in the future, and why this one? Last week I returned from a sports youth camp …", "about": "the youth camp", "vocab": "", "bg": "This task invites a personal or contextual answer about hobbies. Use concrete examples, not unsupported universal claims. Distinguish your own experience from national facts.", "qs": [{"t": "How do you and your friends spend free time in your region?", "m": [["We often go for walks, play sport or meet at cafés in our region.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["My friends and I spend free time cycling, watching films or chatting.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."], ["We enjoy sports facilities, parks and spending time together after school.", "Gives a concrete action or personal detail relevant to the question."]]}, {"t": "Which hobbies are popular with teens in Russia?", "m": [["Popular hobbies include gaming, music, sport and drawing.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Many teenagers enjoy dancing, photography and team sports.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Among my friends, reading, gaming and playing musical instruments are common.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What new hobby would you like to try in the future, and why this one?", "m": [["I would like to try photography because I enjoy noticing interesting details.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I want to learn to play the guitar because I love music.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I would choose rock climbing because it looks challenging and exciting.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}], "sets": [[["Where was the youth camp?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["How long did you stay there?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["What activities did you enjoy most?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["How many teenagers attended the camp?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["What did you learn there?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Who supervised the activities?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."]], [["What was the accommodation like?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Did you make any new friends?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["Would you like to go back next year?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]]]}, {"n": 25, "name": "Morris", "g": "his", "subject": "Environment protection", "body": "… You know that I’ve always been involved in various environmental activities. What are the environmental issues that are most pressing in Russia today? What are the ways in which people in Russia try to protect the environment? What else do you think people in your country can do to help protect the environment? Yesterday I watched a very interesting documentary …", "about": "the documentary he liked", "vocab": "", "bg": "Environmental challenges differ by region. Good examples include air pollution, waste management and forest fires.", "qs": [{"t": "What are the environmental issues that are most pressing in Russia today?", "m": [["Air pollution and waste management are serious environmental concerns in parts of Russia.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Problems include forest fires, plastic waste and pollution of rivers.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I think protecting forests and reducing pollution are among the main challenges.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What are the ways in which people in Russia try to protect the environment?", "m": [["People take part in clean-up events, recycle where facilities exist and plant trees.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Volunteers organise litter collections and support local environmental campaigns.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Some communities sort waste, protect parks and teach children about conservation.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What else do you think people in your country can do to help protect the environment?", "m": [["People could use public transport more often and reduce single-use plastic.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Better recycling facilities and environmental education would help.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["We should save energy, protect green spaces and support clean-up projects.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}], "sets": [[["What was the documentary about?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Who made it?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."], ["What did you like most about it?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["What is the title of the documentary?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Where did you watch it?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["What did you learn from it?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["How long was the documentary?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["What issue did it focus on?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Would you recommend it to me?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]]]}, {"n": 26, "name": "Victoria", "g": "her", "subject": "Visit to Russia", "body": "… My parents and I want to take a tour across Russia next summer. We need your advice. What cities should we visit, why these? Is it better to travel by rail or by air in Russia? What is the weather like in summer? I’ve passed my Spanish exam! …", "about": "the exam", "vocab": "", "bg": "Russia covers different climate zones. Summer weather and transport preferences depend on the route and region.", "qs": [{"t": "What cities should we visit, why these?", "m": [["I would recommend Moscow for its museums and Saint Petersburg for its architecture.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["You should visit Kazan because it has a rich cultural history and interesting sights.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I suggest Moscow and Saint Petersburg because both offer famous landmarks and museums.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}, {"t": "Is it better to travel by rail or by air in Russia?", "m": [["Rail is great for shorter journeys because you can see the countryside, but flying is faster over long distances.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["In such a large country, flying is often better for distant destinations because it saves time.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I prefer trains for comfort and views, although planes are more practical for very long trips.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What is the weather like in summer?", "m": [["Summer weather varies: it can be warm in central Russia but cooler in the north.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["In many Russian cities summer is pleasantly warm, although conditions depend on the region.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["You can expect warm weather in some areas and cooler temperatures elsewhere because Russia is so large.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}], "sets": [[["Which subject was the exam in?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["How long did the exam last?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["Which part was the most difficult?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["How did you prepare for the exam?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["Were there any unexpected questions?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["How did you feel afterwards?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]], [["Was it a written or an oral exam?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["How many questions did you have to answer?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["What advice would you give someone taking it?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 27, "name": "Carol", "g": "her", "subject": "Eating out", "body": "… My friends and I enjoy eating out a lot. There are so many nice cafés around! How often do you eat out? Is eating out popular with young people in Russia, and why or why not? What traditional Russian dishes do you like? I’ve just returned from a hiking trip …", "about": "the hiking trip", "vocab": "", "bg": "This task invites a personal or contextual answer about eating out. Use concrete examples, not unsupported universal claims. Distinguish your own experience from national facts.", "qs": [{"t": "How often do you eat out?", "m": [["I eat out about once a week, usually with friends.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["I rarely eat out because my family usually cooks at home.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."], ["I go to a café or restaurant a couple of times a month.", "Provides the specific quantity, frequency, time or place requested."]]}, {"t": "Is eating out popular with young people in Russia, and why or why not?", "m": [["Yes, many young people like cafés because they are convenient places to meet friends.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["Eating out is quite popular, especially in cities where there are many affordable cafés.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["It depends on the area and budget, but plenty of young people enjoy eating out socially.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}, {"t": "What traditional Russian dishes do you like?", "m": [["I enjoy pelmeni and borscht because they are filling and tasty.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["My favourite traditional dishes are blini and shchi.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I like buckwheat porridge and homemade pelmeni.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}], "sets": [[["Where did you go hiking?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["How long did the trip last?", "Asks for duration related to the target."], ["Who went with you?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."]], [["What route did you follow?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Where did you stay overnight?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["What was the most difficult part?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["What was the weather like on the hike?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["What equipment did you take?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["What did you enjoy most about the trip?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]]]}, {"n": 28, "name": "Jack", "g": "his", "subject": "Leisure time", "body": "… My friends and I regularly go to the theatre. Is it popular with teenagers to go to the theatre in your country? Are you a theatregoer? Who is your favourite Russian playwright, and why? I’ve bought a new computer game …", "about": "the computer game", "vocab": "", "bg": "This task invites a personal or contextual answer about leisure time. Use concrete examples, not unsupported universal claims. Distinguish your own experience from national facts.", "qs": [{"t": "Is it popular with teenagers to go to the theatre in your country?", "m": [["Some teenagers enjoy theatre, although cinema and online entertainment are often more popular.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Theatre is popular with some young people, especially when schools organise visits.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Many teenagers go to the theatre occasionally, but not everyone is interested in it.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "Are you a theatregoer?", "m": [["Yes, I enjoy theatre and try to see a play a few times a year.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I do not go very often, but I enjoyed the last school theatre trip.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I am not a regular theatregoer, although I would like to see more performances.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "Who is your favourite Russian playwright, and why?", "m": [["My favourite is Anton Chekhov because his plays portray people realistically.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I admire Aleksandr Ostrovsky because his plays explore family and society.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I like Chekhov because his characters and their relationships are interesting.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}], "sets": [[["What is the new computer game called?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["What is it about?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Can you play it with friends?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]], [["What type of game is it?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Which platform do you play it on?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."], ["What do you like most about the game?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."]], [["Does the game have different difficulty levels?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["How many players can take part?", "Asks for a new quantity related to the target."], ["Why did you decide to buy it?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."]]]}, {"n": 29, "name": "Chris", "g": "his", "subject": "Russian science", "body": "… Yesterday our school teacher told us a lot about Russian scientific inventions. What is the most famous Russian invention? Why is it important to study science at school? What Russian scientist do you think a foreigner should learn about, and why? I’ve just bought a present for my brother …", "about": "the present", "vocab": "", "bg": "Sputnik 1, launched in 1957, was the first artificial Earth satellite. Distinguish an invention from a scientific achievement.", "qs": [{"t": "What is the most famous Russian invention?", "m": [["I think the first artificial satellite, Sputnik 1, is one of Russia’s most famous inventions or achievements.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["The early Soviet space programme is famous, especially the launch of Sputnik 1.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["I would name Sputnik 1 because it was the first artificial satellite to orbit Earth.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "Why is it important to study science at school?", "m": [["Studying science helps us understand how the world works and solve problems.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["Science is important because it develops logical thinking and practical skills.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["It helps students make informed decisions and learn about modern technology.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}, {"t": "What Russian scientist do you think a foreigner should learn about, and why?", "m": [["I recommend learning about Dmitri Mendeleev because his periodic table transformed chemistry.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["A foreigner should know about Mikhail Lomonosov because he contributed to several scientific fields.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."], ["I would choose Konstantin Tsiolkovsky because his ideas helped develop the theory of spaceflight.", "Gives a relevant reason and directly addresses the reason requested."]]}], "sets": [[["What present did you buy for your brother?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Why did you choose it?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."], ["When are you going to give it to him?", "Asks for timing or frequency not already given in the email."]], [["Where did you find the present?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["What does it look like?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Is it connected with one of his hobbies?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]], [["Did you ask anyone for help choosing the present?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["What colour is it?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["How are you planning to wrap it?", "Relevant to the target and requests information not supplied in the email."]]]}, {"n": 30, "name": "Alice", "g": "her", "subject": "Russian cuisine", "body": "… Our school teacher asked us to do a project on national dishes of different countries. I want to write about the Russian cuisine. What traditional dishes are popular in your country? What national dish is the easiest to cook? What ingredients are needed to cook it? I want to start taking singing lessons …", "about": "the singing lessons", "vocab": "", "bg": "Pelmeni are filled dumplings; blini are thin pancakes. For a recipe prompt, give actual ingredients for the chosen dish.", "qs": [{"t": "What traditional dishes are popular in your country?", "m": [["Pelmeni, borscht and blini are well-known traditional dishes in Russia.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Popular traditional foods include shchi, buckwheat porridge and pelmeni.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Many people enjoy blini, soups and dumplings as part of Russian cuisine.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What national dish is the easiest to cook?", "m": [["I think blini are among the easiest traditional dishes to make because the recipe is simple.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Buckwheat porridge is easy to cook because it needs only a few basic ingredients.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["For a beginner, blini are fairly easy because the batter is quick to prepare.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}, {"t": "What ingredients are needed to cook it?", "m": [["For blini, you need flour, eggs, milk and a little oil.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["Buckwheat porridge needs buckwheat, water and a little salt.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."], ["To make simple blini, you need milk, flour, eggs and some oil.", "Supplies relevant specific information answering this question."]]}], "sets": [[["Where will you take singing lessons?", "Requests a place linked to the target; check that it is not already known."], ["How often will you have them?", "Asks for timing or frequency not already given in the email."], ["Who will teach you?", "Asks for a person linked to the target, not a different topic."]], [["What kind of songs would you like to learn?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Will the lessons be individual or in a group?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."], ["How long will each lesson last?", "Asks for duration related to the target."]], [["Why did you decide to start singing lessons?", "Asks for a new reason connected to the specified target."], ["What vocal skills do you want to improve?", "Asks for a specific detail about the required target."], ["Are you planning to perform in public?", "A meaningful yes/no question about the target and unknown information."]]]}];
window.W37RU=[{"title": "Traditional Russian Toys", "name": "Sophie", "g": "her", "body": "...Last week I visited a toy museum in my town and saw dolls from different countries. Are there any traditional Russian toys? What is the most famous one and how is it made? Do children still play with traditional toys nowadays? At the weekend I started collecting dolls from different countries as a hobby...", "about": "her doll collection", "sup": ["Traditional Russian toys include the matryoshka, Dymkovo clay toys and Bogorodskaya wooden toys.", "The matryoshka is a set of wooden dolls that fit one inside another.", "Traditional toys were often made and painted by hand.", "Nowadays traditional toys are popular souvenirs for tourists.", "Making traditional toys is considered a form of Russian folk art."]}, {"title": "New Year", "name": "Oliver", "g": "his", "body": "...In Britain we celebrate Christmas as our main winter holiday. What is the most important winter holiday in Russia? How do families usually celebrate it? Who brings presents to children in Russia? Last weekend my family put up our Christmas tree and decorated the house...", "about": "decorating his Christmas tree", "sup": ["New Year is the main winter holiday in Russia, celebrated on the night of the 31st of December.", "Families gather together, decorate a New Year tree and watch fireworks at midnight.", "Ded Moroz (Grandfather Frost) and his granddaughter Snegurochka bring presents to children.", "People make a wish at midnight when the clock strikes twelve.", "Christmas in Russia is celebrated later, on the 7th of January."]}, {"title": "Maslenitsa", "name": "Megan", "g": "her", "body": "...In Britain we have Pancake Day before Lent. I heard that Russia has a similar tradition. What is Maslenitsa and when is it celebrated? What do people usually eat and do during this holiday? Why do people burn a straw doll at the end of the week? Last weekend I made pancakes with my family for Pancake Day...", "about": "her Pancake Day", "sup": ["Maslenitsa is a traditional Russian holiday celebrating the end of winter.", "It is celebrated during the last week before Lent, usually in February or March.", "The main food of the holiday is bliny (pancakes), which symbolise the sun.", "People visit family and friends, sing songs and take part in outdoor games.", "At the end of the week people burn a straw doll to say goodbye to winter and welcome spring."]}, {"title": "Ballet in Russia", "name": "Grace", "g": "her", "body": "...I've just started ballet lessons at a dance school. I've heard that Russian ballet is famous all over the world. Why is Russian ballet so highly respected? What are the most famous Russian ballet theatres? Do you know any famous Russian dancers? Last week I performed in my first ballet show...", "about": "her ballet show", "sup": ["Russian ballet is famous all over the world for its high level of skill.", "The Bolshoi Theatre in Moscow and the Mariinsky Theatre in Saint Petersburg are the most famous ballet venues.", "The composer Tchaikovsky wrote music for famous ballets such as \"Swan Lake\" and \"The Nutcracker\".", "Many world-famous dancers, such as Anna Pavlova, came from Russia.", "Children can study ballet at special schools from a young age."]}, {"title": "The Golden Ring of Russia", "name": "Daniel", "g": "his", "body": "...I'm doing a school project about historic towns in different countries. I've heard about a famous route of old Russian towns. What is the Golden Ring of Russia? Which towns does it include? Why do tourists like visiting them? Last weekend I visited a historic town near my home with my class...", "about": "the historic town he visited", "sup": ["The Golden Ring is a group of ancient historic towns to the north-east of Moscow.", "It includes cities such as Suzdal, Vladimir and Sergiev Posad.", "The towns are famous for their old churches, monasteries and kremlins.", "The route shows the traditional architecture and culture of medieval Russia.", "Many tourists travel around the Golden Ring to learn about Russian history."]}, {"title": "Space Exploration and Yuri Gagarin", "name": "Tom", "g": "his", "body": "...I'm really interested in space exploration. I know that Russia has achieved a lot in this field. Who was Yuri Gagarin and what did he do? When is Cosmonautics Day celebrated in Russia? Why is his achievement still important today? Last week our class visited a planetarium...", "about": "the visit to the planetarium", "sup": ["Yuri Gagarin was the first person to travel into space, on the 12th of April 1961.", "His flight lasted 108 minutes and he orbited the Earth once.", "The 12th of April is celebrated in Russia as Cosmonautics Day.", "Russia has a long history of achievements in space exploration.", "Gagarin's flight made him a national hero and a symbol of human achievement."]}, {"title": "Education in Russia", "name": "Ryan", "g": "his", "body": "...We're doing a project comparing school systems in different countries. What is school education like in Russia? At what age do children start school? What exams do students take at the end of school? Last month I started preparing for my final exams...", "about": "his exam preparation", "sup": ["Children in Russia usually start school at the age of 6 or 7.", "School education lasts 11 years and is divided into primary, middle and senior levels.", "At the end of school, students take exams called the OGE and the EGE.", "Education in Russian schools is free and compulsory.", "After school, students can continue their studies at colleges or universities."]}, {"title": "Universities in Russia", "name": "Zoe", "g": "her", "body": "...I'm starting to think about which university to apply to. What are the most famous universities in Russia? What subjects are they well-known for? Is it difficult to get a place there? Last week I went to a university open day in my city...", "about": "the university open day", "sup": ["Moscow State University is the oldest and most famous university in Russia.", "It was founded in 1755 by Mikhail Lomonosov.", "Other well-known universities include Saint Petersburg State University and MGIMO.", "Russian universities offer courses in a wide range of subjects, from science to humanities.", "Getting a place at a top university is usually very competitive."]}, {"title": "Russian Literature", "name": "Kate", "g": "her", "body": "...In our English lessons we're studying classic novels. What Russian writers or books are famous all over the world? Which Russian book would you recommend to a foreign teenager? Do you enjoy reading in your free time? Last month I started keeping a reading diary...", "about": "her reading diary", "sup": ["Russia has produced many world-famous writers, such as Tolstoy, Dostoevsky and Chekhov.", "Their books deal with deep questions about life, morality and society.", "\"War and Peace\" and \"Crime and Punishment\" are known all over the world.", "Reading classic literature helps to understand Russian history and culture.", "I enjoy reading because it develops imagination and widens one's knowledge."]}, {"title": "Day of Family, Love and Fidelity", "name": "Emma", "g": "her", "body": "...In Russia there's a holiday called the Day of Family, Love and Fidelity. Do you have a similar holiday in your country? What does your family usually do to celebrate special family days? Why do you think it's important to have such holidays? Last weekend I helped my grandmother in her garden and learned a lot about plants...", "about": "her gardening experience", "sup": ["This holiday is celebrated on the 8th of July.", "It celebrates family values, love and loyalty.", "The symbol of the holiday is a camomile (daisy).", "Families usually spend the day together, have a picnic or a family dinner.", "It reminds people how important family bonds are."]}, {"title": "Constitution Day", "name": "Jack", "g": "his", "body": "...We recently studied the British Constitution at school. Does Russia have a special day connected with its Constitution? What do people usually do on this day? Do you think it's important for young people to know their country's main law? Last month I joined a debate club at school and it's really exciting...", "about": "his debate club", "sup": ["The Constitution of Russia was adopted on the 12th of December, 1993.", "It is the main law of the country.", "The Constitution guarantees people's rights and freedoms.", "Schools often organise lessons or quizzes about the Constitution on this day.", "It's important for young people to know their rights and duties."]}, {"title": "Russian State Symbols", "name": "Lily", "g": "her", "body": "...In our history lessons we discussed national symbols like the flag and the anthem. What are the state symbols of Russia? What do the colours of the Russian flag mean? Do people in Russia celebrate a special day for state symbols? Last week I took part in a school quiz about British history and won a prize...", "about": "her school quiz", "sup": ["The main state symbols are the flag, the anthem and the coat of arms.", "The Russian flag has three colours: white, blue and red.", "White stands for peace, blue for loyalty, and red for strength/courage.", "The coat of arms shows a two-headed eagle.", "The national anthem is played at official ceremonies and sports events."]}, {"title": "Russian Science and Scientists", "name": "Ben", "g": "his", "body": "...We learned about Isaac Newton at school and how he changed science. Are there any famous Russian scientists you know about? What did Mikhail Lomonosov contribute to Russian science and education? Would you like to become a scientist yourself? Last week our class visited a science museum...", "about": "the science museum", "sup": ["Mikhail Lomonosov was a famous Russian scientist, poet and educator.", "He made discoveries in chemistry, physics and astronomy.", "He founded Moscow State University in 1755.", "He believed that education was the key to the country's progress.", "Russian science has produced many outstanding scientists and inventions."]}, {"title": "Peter the Great", "name": "Alice", "g": "her", "body": "...I'm doing a school project about famous rulers who built new cities. Who was Peter the Great and why did he found Saint Petersburg? What makes this city special today? Have you ever visited it? Last weekend my family and I went on a trip to an old castle...", "about": "the trip to the castle", "sup": ["Peter the Great was a Russian tsar who modernised the country.", "He founded Saint Petersburg in 1703 as a \"window to Europe\".", "The city became the capital of Russia for over 200 years.", "Saint Petersburg is famous for its palaces, museums and canals.", "The Hermitage Museum and Peterhof are must-see places there."]}, {"title": "Natural Wonders of Russia", "name": "Nathan", "g": "his", "body": "...In geography lessons we're learning about famous natural landmarks around the world. What are the most impressive natural landmarks in Russia? Why is Russia's nature so varied? Have you ever visited any of these places? Last weekend I went camping in a national park near my town...", "about": "his camping trip", "sup": ["Russia is the largest country in the world and has a great variety of natural landscapes.", "Lake Baikal is the deepest and oldest freshwater lake on Earth.", "The Ural Mountains divide the country into European and Asian parts.", "Kamchatka is famous for its active volcanoes and geysers.", "Many natural areas in Russia are protected as national parks and nature reserves."]}, {"title": "Flag Day", "name": "Harry", "g": "his", "body": "...We have Union Jack Day in some parts of Britain to celebrate our flag. Does Russia have a similar holiday for its flag? What do the colours of the Russian flag stand for? How do people usually celebrate this day? Last month our school organised a small festival with flags from different countries...", "about": "the school festival", "sup": ["The Day of the Russian Flag is celebrated on the 22nd of August.", "The flag has three horizontal stripes: white, blue and red.", "It symbolises peace, loyalty and courage.", "People often take part in parades and festivals on this day.", "The flag is an important symbol of national identity."]}, {"title": "The Battle of the Ice", "name": "Ethan", "g": "his", "body": "...I'm reading about famous medieval battles for my history project. I heard about a battle that took place on ice in Russian history. What was the Battle of the Ice and who fought in it? Why is Alexander Nevsky considered a national hero in Russia? Have you ever visited any places connected with this battle? Last week I watched a documentary about medieval knights...", "about": "the documentary", "sup": ["The Battle of the Ice took place on Lake Peipus in 1242.", "Prince Alexander Nevsky led the Russian army against the German knights (Teutonic Order).", "The battle got its name because it was fought on the frozen lake.", "Alexander Nevsky is remembered as a national hero and a symbol of courage.", "The victory stopped the invasion from the west."]}, {"title": "The Battle of Kulikovo", "name": "Chloe", "g": "her", "body": "...In our history class we're comparing famous battles from different countries. What was the Battle of Kulikovo and why is it so important in Russian history? Who led the Russian army? Is this battle still remembered today? Last weekend I went to a historical re-enactment event near my town...", "about": "the historical re-enactment event", "sup": ["The Battle of Kulikovo took place in 1380.", "Prince Dmitry Donskoy led the Russian army against the Mongol-Tatar forces.", "The battle was a turning point in the struggle against Mongol rule.", "It showed that the Russian princedoms could unite against a common enemy.", "Dmitry Donskoy became a symbol of Russian unity and bravery."]}];
